"""Generate scientific report and source-to-claim map from retained tables."""
from .core import *
from .analysis import position_geometry

def main():
 read=lambda n:pd.read_csv(OUT/'tables'/f'{n}.csv');position_geometry(read('position_predictions')).to_csv(OUT/'tables/position_geometry.csv',index=False);summary=read('endpoint_summary');counts=read('endpoint_counts');b=read('block_transfer');s=read('switch_costs');g=read('geometry');joint=read('joint_descriptive');p=read('paired_intervals');math=read('mathematical_checks')
 rows=[]
 for (seed,arm,window,cue),x in b.groupby(['seed','arm','window','practiced']):
  rows.append(dict(seed=seed,arm=arm,window=window,practiced=cue,practiced_gain=x.practiced_gain.mean(),unpracticed_gain=x.unpracticed_gain.mean(),specificity=x.specificity.mean(),floor_blocks=int(x.floor_at_start.sum()),blocks=len(x),above_floor_blocks=int((~x.floor_at_start).sum())))
 window=pd.DataFrame(rows);window.to_csv(OUT/'tables/window_seed_effects.csv',index=False);wi=[]
 for key,x in window.groupby(['arm','window','practiced']):
  for metric in ['practiced_gain','unpracticed_gain','specificity']:
   mean,lo,hi=interval(x[metric]);wi.append(dict(zip(['arm','window','practiced'],key),metric=metric,mean=mean,ci_low=lo,ci_high=hi,n=20))
 pd.DataFrame(wi).to_csv(OUT/'tables/window_intervals.csv',index=False)
 def val(arm,k,cue,metric='ce'):
  return summary[(summary.arm==arm)&(summary['update']==k)&(summary.cue==cue)&(summary.subgroup=='all')&(summary.metric==metric)].iloc[0]
 def count(arm,k,cue):return counts[(counts.arm==arm)&(counts['update']==k)&(counts.cue==cue)&(counts.subgroup=='all')].iloc[0]
 lines=['# Shared sequence learning with centered context','',
 'Both controlled Linear arms acquired A/B and generalized to C. Centering guaranteed C–Mixed equivalence while preserving A/B geometry and early context-specific learning. It did **not** uniquely enable C success: the trainable-common-input baseline also succeeded. Persistent separate learning is not established.','',
 'Twenty paired seeds per arm received exactly330 A10/B10 updates (13,200 scientific updates), with no C/Mixed exposure in the loss and no selection on their evaluations. Both arms started at g=0 with identical d and all other weights. Initial Wh spectral norm=.9 was applied once; it was free thereafter. The normalized source direct Generator draws were reused, with d=(old W_A−old W_B)/2. These are new controlled baselines, not reruns of the earlier Standard initialization or the unnormalized High cohort.','',
 'The actual update is h_t=W_h h_(t−1)+W_token x_t+b_ih+b_hh+g(c_A+c_B)+d(c_A−c_B), z_t=W_o h_t+b_o. h0=0; seven teacher-forced current tokens [0,1,2,0,3,1,2], targets [1,2,0,3,1,2,3]. No history/position features. Standard g is trainable; Centered g is an exact zero buffer. Both use the same g/d coordinates. CE+.2 execution loss, detached confidence, two-parameter monotonic policy, Adam(.005, default moments/epsilon), and joint gradient clipping1 are imported unchanged. Centered has156 trainable model parameters, Standard164, plus2 policy parameters each; the unused C column is fixed zero.','',
 'All scheduled states0..330, seeds and positions were retained. Evaluations are frozen between updates and cannot change training. Figures and intervals use whole trained seeds (10,000 bootstrap draws; seed20260925), never positions as independent networks. Intervals are pointwise descriptive, not simultaneous or multiplicity-adjusted.','',
 '## Acquisition and generalization','',
 '| Arm | Update | A CE | B CE | Mixed CE | C CE | Strong A/B | C accuracy | C success |',
 '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ARMS:
  for k in PROBES:
   n=counts[(counts.arm==arm)&(counts['update']==k)&(counts.cue=='C')&(counts.subgroup=='strong_familiar')].iloc[0]['n'];lines.append(f'| {arm} | {k} | '+ ' | '.join(f'{val(arm,k,c)["mean"]:.6f}' for c in ['A','B','Mixed','C'])+f' | {n}/20 | {val(arm,k,"C","accuracy")["mean"]:.4f} | {count(arm,k,"C").strong_performance}/20 |')
 lines+=['', 'Strong familiar learning means CE≤.5 and accuracy≥6/7 independently in both A and B. C success uses the same per-cue rule. Exact accuracies, confidence intervals, all20 and familiar-only subgroup summaries are in endpoint_summary.csv and endpoint_counts.csv. All20 qualify by120 in both arms; consequently later subgroup summaries equal the full cohort. No endpoint or hyperparameter was selected from C.\n']
 for arm in ARMS:
  r=val(arm,330,'C');lines.append(f'At330 {arm} C CE={r["mean"]:.9f}, 95% seed CI[{r.ci_low:.9f},{r.ci_high:.9f}]; C accuracy=1.0, no seeds above ln(4).')
 r=p[(p['update']==330)&(p.cue=='C')&(p.metric=='ce')].iloc[0];lines+=['',f'The paired Centered−Standard C CE difference at330 is {r["mean"]:.9f}, CI[{r.ci_low:.9f},{r.ci_high:.9f}]. This is a small loss advantage among already successful models; it does not establish a qualitative acquisition/generalization dissociation. The old unnormalized C-failure diagnostic used a different initialization and is a historical reference only.','',
 '## Learning and representation','',
 'Actual practiced loss has large early discontinuous switch jumps (Figure1). Figure2 follows frozen A/B/Mixed/C jointly. Switch cost is incoming−outgoing CE at identical pre-switch weights; initial-bias-adjusted costs and absolute/signed A/B gaps are retained separately. At state330 no next B block exists, so it is end-censored. Switch costs shrink toward zero as acquisition reaches floor; subtracting initial A/B asymmetry need not tend to zero. A jump in practiced losses alone is not proof of separate skills.','',
 'Block effects use frozen start/end states: own_gain=L_own(start)−L_own(end), cross_gain=L_other(start)−L_other(end), specificity=own_gain−cross_gain. Negative gains are retained, with no unstable ratios. Early block-averaged specificity is:\n']
 for arm in ARMS:
  for cue in ['A','B']:
   r=pd.DataFrame(wi).query('arm==@arm and window=="early" and practiced==@cue and metric=="specificity"').iloc[0];lines.append(f'- {arm}, {cue} practice: {r["mean"]:.6f} nats, CI[{r.ci_low:.6f},{r.ci_high:.6f}].')
 lines+=['', 'Each network in both arms has at least one above-floor positive A specificity and one above-floor positive B specificity in early blocks ending≤100. This is descriptive directional evidence, not a new splitting threshold or confirmation of the original joint functional gate. A positive own-minus-cross difference may include deterioration; raw gains remain visible. Neither arm has bidirectional above-floor sign evidence in the late window.']
 for arm in ARMS:
  bb=b[(b.arm==arm)&(b.window=='late')];gg=g[(g.arm==arm)&(g['update']==330)];lines.append(f'{arm}: {bb.floor_at_start.sum()}/{len(bb)} late blocks already start with both familiar losses≤.05. At330 mean hidden separation={gg.hidden_separation.mean():.6f}, centered-logit separation={gg.centered_logit_separation.mean():.6f}, centroid distance={gg.hidden_centroid_distance.mean():.6f}, ||d||={gg.d_norm.mean():.6f}, ||g||={gg.g_norm.mean():.6f}.')
 lines+=['', 'All20 per arm retain hidden and centered-logit separation above the prespecified numerical tolerance at330. Much separation was already present at initialization, so this is retention of context dependence, not evidence that separation was newly learned. Nonzero distance is a numerical fact, not meaningful independent skills. The descriptive joint count of strong A/B + C success + nonzero separation + early bidirectional block signs is20/20 per arm at120/170/330; using late above-floor signs it is0/20. These counts must not be described as persistent splitting. Restored-Adam one-update diagnostics were not requested or run; the inherited joint splitting criterion remains unassessed.','',
 '## Mathematics and numerical checks','',
 'Let H0 be the token/bias trajectory, U_t=W_h U_(t−1)+g, V_t=W_h V_(t−1)+d, with U0=V0=0. Then H_A=H0+U+V, H_B=H0+U−V, H_M=H0+U and H_C=H0. In Centered, U=0: C=Mixed=(A+B)/2 in hidden states and logits at every position. Thus CE_C=CE_M≤(CE_A+CE_B)/2 by convexity. A/B can differ through V. The ordinary C input naturally produces H0 under this imposed constraint; no fitted hidden state or logit rescue was used. This construction does not show spontaneous discovery of a retrieval policy.','',
 '**Qualification:** the theorem guarantees the CE bound, not the additional accuracy≥6/7 cutoff. A retained test counterexample has A/B each meeting both criteria but a midpoint with5/7 correct. Here C accuracy success is measured, not inferred. The PRD’s broad guarantee is therefore interpreted precisely as a loss guarantee.','',
 f'All92,680 position checks pass across40×331 states. Maximum double midpoint logit residual={math.double_logit_midpoint_error.max():.3g}; tolerance=1e−10+1e−12×scale fixed before training. Maximum float32 midpoint logit residual={math.float32_logit_midpoint_error.max():.3g}, within the inherited64eps absolute-summand/recurrence-propagation bound. CE uses twice the logit allowance. Centered C and Mixed hidden/logit arrays are bitwise identical in native float32 and double at every state; output probabilities also match. Third-channel weights are identically zero by construction.','',
 'The common sequence baseline is accessible without familiar cues in this design, but “shared sequence computation” is an operational description of the token/bias trajectory, not a recovered cognitive retrieval algorithm. Wh spectral norm changes after initialization as permitted. Standard also began with no common cue drive and learned a relatively small g; its C success cannot be attributed solely to constraining g.','',
 '## Figures and source map','']
 for i,name,title in [(1,'01_actual_training_loss','Actual pre-update A10/B10 loss: full330 and first100'),(2,'02_frozen_cue_learning','Frozen A/B/Mixed/C acquisition, symlog CE'),(3,'03_signed_switch_costs','Signed same-weight switch costs and baseline diagnostic'),(4,'04_within_cross_context_gains','Raw within/cross gains over blocks, gain-pair insets'),(5,'05_representation_and_learning','Separate hidden/output geometry and signed learning specificity')]:lines+= [f'**Figure{i}. {title}.**',f'![Figure{i}](figures/{name}.png)','']
 lines+=['PNG and SVG files use every seed; no unsuccessful observations were removed. Figure1 remains linear scale; other symlog scales retain zero/negative values as labeled. Exact inputs and bootstrap means/bounds are in tables/. Figures regenerate without model evaluation.','',
 '## Conclusions and limits','',
 'A Linear RNN can retain distinct A/B trajectories and early context-specific learning effects while accurately predicting under a never-trained third cue. Both arms do so in this controlled normalized setting. Centering provides a mathematical CE guarantee and slightly lower C CE; a selective rescue relative to a failing Standard arm was not observed. Persistent separate learning and the full human pattern remain unestablished, especially once late losses reach floor. No architecture, hyperparameter, stopping point or criterion was adjusted to favor the outcome.']
 (OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
 claims=[('C1','Paired identical initialization and g-only manipulation','checkpoint_registry.csv','core.py'),('C2','All40 complete fixed budget','training_trajectories.csv','run.py'),('C3','Both arms acquire and generalize; no qualitative selective C rescue','endpoint_summary.csv','analysis.py'),('C4','Centered C/Mixed identity and Jensen CE bound','mathematical_checks.csv','core.py'),('C5','Early preferential learning is compatible with transfer','block_transfer.csv','analysis.py'),('C6','Late inference limited by floor','window_seed_effects.csv','report.py'),('C7','Geometry persists but does not establish independent learning','geometry.csv','run.py'),('C8','Paired small C CE advantage','paired_intervals.csv','analysis.py'),('C9','Joint early-sign counts not persistent splitting','joint_descriptive.csv','analysis.py'),('C10','Switch costs signed and same-weight; end-censored330','switch_costs.csv','analysis.py')]
 pd.DataFrame([dict(claim_id=cid,claim=claim,source='tables/'+table,source_sha256=sha(OUT/'tables'/table),implementation='experiments/centered_context_linear/'+impl,limitation='Descriptive seed inference; original functional splitting gate unassessed' if cid in ['C5','C6','C7','C9','C10'] else 'New controlled normalized cohort; no claim of spontaneous retrieval') for cid,claim,table,impl in claims]).to_csv(OUT/'tables/claim_ledger.csv',index=False)
 (OUT/'RESEARCHER_HANDOFF.md').write_text('''# Researcher teach-back

The only paired manipulation is whether an initially zero common cue vector g may learn. Both arms share signed contrast d. Inputs A/B supply +d/−d; Centered Mixed and C supply no cue drive. The shared token/bias recurrence consequently predicts the exact A/B logit midpoint, with a Jensen bound on CE. Accuracy needs separate measurement.

Both arms acquire A/B (20/20 by120), retain substantial geometry and predict C correctly (20/20 by100). Centered330 C CE=.000083 versus Standard .001866. This does not yield the proposed selective acquisition/generalization dissociation. Early practice favors the practiced context while also transferring. Late above-floor evidence is inadequate; geometry and floor-limited loss changes cannot establish independent skills. Original splitting criterion unchanged and unassessed.

Read REPORT.md and five figures first. tables/training_trajectories.csv contains13,200 actual pre-update measurements; frozen_evaluations.csv contains52,960 cue cells; position_predictions.csv retains370,720 rows with all hidden states, logits and probabilities. geometry.csv and block_transfer.csv separate representation from functional measurements. generalization.csv retains all800 prespecified endpoint/cue rows. checkpoint_registry.csv hashes40 bundles containing13,240 full model/policy/Adam states. mathematical_checks.csv records92,680 position controls. claim_ledger.csv links claims to exact source hashes.

Reproduction is read-only: use experiments.centered_context_linear.verify and optional --regenerate with a new empty destination. Never rerun run.py: the fixed budget is complete. Unnormalized prior C-failure results and earlier normalized initialization are historical references, not pooled arms. The experiment changed parameter coordinates and g initialization intentionally. No novel retrieval policy, persistent separate learning or complete human phenotype is established.
''')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
